From 940ebc186a5b5a0c5379c412f952dbdb96fb1249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali Zuccato <ali@myendobuddy.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 20:41:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix premium features: real grocery list, honest empty states
 for Treatments & Visualizations

1. Meal Plans: Generate Shopping List button was a no-op that just
   flashed a fake success message. Added real ingredient data to every
   phase meal (regular + flare-up + nut-free variants) and a working
   generator that aggregates/dedupes ingredients from the meals
   currently shown, with a checkable list and copy-to-clipboard.

2. Treatment Response Dashboard: was rendering a hardcoded
   MOCK_TREATMENTS array (Norethindrone, PT, Ibuprofen, Lo Loestrin)
   with no backend behind it at all -- no logging UI, no /api
   endpoints, even though medications/medication_entries tables
   already exist unused in the schema. Replaced with an honest empty
   state; component now accepts a treatments prop so real data can
   be wired in once logging exists.

3. Premium Visualizations: Cycle Compare and Correlation Map were
   fully hardcoded (DEFAULT_CORRELATIONS, fixed phase averages).
   Replaced both with honest empty states explaining what's missing
   (lifestyle-factor logging for correlations; more cycle history for
   compare). Pain Forecast already partially used real pattern data --
   left that logic intact but it now also shows an honest empty state
   when no phase_correlation pattern exists yet, instead of always
   rendering with hardcoded phase defaults.
